I go into the neighbourhood cafe.
It is still early in the morning and very quiet.
I walk directly behind the counter.
A woman with a friendly smile is already waiting there.
"Hello, I am Elif," she says in greeting.
"I am Maya," I answer.
"This is my first shift today."
Elif laughs and shakes my hand.
"Welcome to the team, Maya!" she says.
She points to a door at the back of the room.
"You can hang up your jacket there," she explains.
I go into the small room and leave my jacket there.
Then I come back to the counter.
Elif gives me a black apron.
"Here, for you," she says kindly.
I put the apron on and smile.
"Don't worry, we have a lot of time today," Elif says.
"Today you learn to work in the café."
I take a deep breath and am ready for my first day.
